_irNotes: {
	"decision-auth-door": "Iris uses lazy guest sessions with auth.required: false, promote: true, and Google OIDC (identity_signin.cue). Readers enter the gallery or scan screen immediately without a blocking gate; an on-demand Access & Portability modal lets them commit their device-bound guest session or promote it in place to a Passkey or Google account without losing their scanned specimens"
	"decision-camera-scan": "The camera scan screen (/camera) pairs a tab-durable ScanDraft viewfinder with a TrackRequest create form. Storing the active specimen preset, AI model selection (gemini / openai), and collection city in a singleton ScanDraft row (`id = 'draft'`) lets the viewfinder and the nested submit-scan form share state declaratively while 011_owner_writes.sql scopes the resulting TrackRequest insert to auth_uid()"
	"decision-classify-trigger": "Deterministic specimen classification runs via 015_classify_request.sql as an AFTER INSERT ON track_request PL/pgSQL trigger. Reusing NEW.id and NEW.created_at from the incoming track_request row avoids volatile clock/UUID calls inside the trigger body, enforces idempotency on trash_item.request_id, and immediately populates a rich TrashItem row synced to the reader's My Items and IRIS Global galleries"
	"decision-demo-items": "A fresh volume starts with twelve classified waste specimens, four disposal places, translations, and news in 020_demo_items.sql. An empty recycling guide cannot demonstrate sorting streams, material recovery values, or multilingual instructions to a first-time guest"
	"decision-design-identity": "Iris Field Guide palette in DESIGN.md with closed light and dark token sets. All colours and dimensions resolve through CSS custom properties in shell/design.css with WCAG AA contrast (>= 4.5:1) in both appearances"
	"decision-detail-tabs": "The specimen detail screen organizes inspection into three tabs via a tab-durable DetailView entity and nested live queries. Wrapping the specimen query inside the seeded detail_view row (`id = 'view'`) keeps all three inspection panes (`discard`, `details`, `nearby`) inside trash_item's scope so nested `trash_item_translation` (`item_id=eq.{id}`) and `disposal_place` (`material_type=eq.{label}`) queries bind the specimen's fields directly while CSS switches panes by `data-tab=\"{tab}\"`"
	"decision-driver": "Acceptance ledger clauses that a single-session visual walk cannot decide are verified by three automated instruments: tests/screens.test.ts over mounted screens and pure Jessie handlers, tests/ledger.ts over multi-session guest tokens at integrate, and tests/verify.ts over live browser journeys. Mounting screens on posed rows via @bonisoft3/omnishell/test/screen-harness.ts exercises tab-durable state folds, 80-character search query caps, save state stamps, and two-tap <details> destructive disclosures deterministically at sayt test, while the multi-session cluster driver and browser verification journeys exercise cross-session RLS, request_id idempotency, and end-to-end navigation"
	"decision-escape-hatches": "Camera capture and local MediaPipe segmentation run in an isolation: \"realm\" unit (camera-lens) with grants: [\"camera\"] and SHA-384-pinned CDN assets. Rather than reaching for ambient host-DOM authority (host-dom) or vendoring multi-megabyte WebAssembly/TFLite binaries into git, shell/units/camera-lens/index.html runs inside an opaque-origin sandboxed iframe with delegated camera access (grants: [\"camera\"]), verifies @mediapipe/tasks-vision@0.10.32 and magic_touch.tflite via SHA-384 Subresource Integrity before execution, and communicates with the host exclusively through its typed ScanDraft read port and capture raise port handled by the pure Jessie scan_draft reducer"
	"decision-gallery-workspace": "The gallery workspace state (active tab and desktop preview selection) lives in a tab-durable GalleryView entity updated by a pure Jessie handler. Keeping tab and preview_id in a single seeded gallery_view row (`id = 'view'`) lets both `` / `` and the nested `` react declaratively without imperative DOM manipulation"
	"decision-inert-first-turn": "Turn 1 establishes the nine core domain entities and two read-only screens (gallery and detail). Interactive tabs, onboarding, camera scan, segmentation overlay, classification triggers, disposal bin registration, and donations arrive turn by turn in Sprints 1–4"
	"decision-intro-and-landing": "Onboarding (/intro) and campaign landing (/lp) are first-class Omnishell routes with declarative state and live specimen feeds. /intro models its 3-step progress bar and slide transitions through a seeded tab-durable OnboardingStep row (`id = 'step'`) and pure Jessie reducer (`onboarding_step.js`), while /lp combines the three acquisition campaign tracks from iris.cleaning/lp with a live `trash_item` specimen showcase"
	"decision-me-row": "Me is a live, private one-row table provisioned synchronously by trigger 013_me_provision.sql. Because Omnishell templates have no session variable placeholder, a private me row scoped to auth_uid() serves as the universal ownership probe across screens"
	"decision-public-read-owner-writes": "Public entities with owner-scoped writes use access: public plus additive RLS policies and column grants in 011_owner_writes.sql. #Access has no \"everyone reads, owner writes\" mode, and widening a private table in SQL would violate the browser mirror contract. Narrowing write columns in 011_owner_writes.sql keeps handle, created_at, and trigger-populated tables safe"
	"decision-responsive-geometry": "Every screen uses container-type: inline-size and @container responsive layouts with min(100%, ...) grid tracks, explicit <img width height> layout-shift guards, and monotonic focus order. Scoping responsive geometry to each screen's inline container rather than viewport @media queries adapts multi-column layouts cleanly whether the desktop sidebar rail (220px) is docked or collapsed into the mobile icon-tab strip, while placing interactive segmentation and model controls in the right-hand submission column on /camera preserves top-to-bottom focus order across all viewports"
	"decision-six-locales-rtl": "All six locales (en, es, pt, ru, he, kk) share an identical message key contract verified by tests/catalogues.test.ts, and Hebrew (/he) uses logical inline CSS properties and bidi isolation. Replacing physical horizontal CSS properties (left, right, margin-left, border-right) with logical properties (inset-inline-start, margin-inline-start, border-inline-end, text-align: start) lets the desktop sidebar rail and multi-column workspaces mirror automatically under dir=\"rtl\" while [data-lang=\"he\"] and unicode-bidi: isolate keep Hebrew specimen translations and news dispatches legible inside any locale"
	"decision-specimens-shipped": "Every specimen image, drop-off hub icon, campaign asset, onboarding illustration, and classification stream icon is content-addressed under pictures/<sha256>.(svg|png), registered in assets/manifest.json (39 entries), attributed on /credits, and verified by tests/pictures.test.ts. Serving static assets from the app's own origin eliminates external image host failures and works identically on local Caddy, Docker release, and Cloudflare edge, while tests/pictures.test.ts enforces 1-to-1 SHA-256 bijection between pictures/, assets/manifest.json, shell/screens/credits.html, and bayt.json"
	"decision-translation-trigger": "On-demand multilingual disposal translations run via 016_translate_item.sql as an AFTER INSERT ON translation_request PL/pgSQL trigger. When a reader submits request-translation on /images/:id, translate_trash_item() looks up the specimen's waste stream and upserts a localized TrashItemTranslation row keyed by (item_id, language) using NEW.id and NEW.created_at, streaming the new localized guide immediately to the How to Discard tab"
}

